<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11683" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεῖδον</span></b> , inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπῐδεῖν,</span>
		aor. 2 with no pres. in use, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφοράω</span> being used instead:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>look away from other things
			at,</i> and so simply, <i>look at,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός</span> or 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔς τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.71
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMar.</u>
				9.2
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόρρωθεν ἀπιδεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Timocl.
					21
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>look away from,</i> and so, <i>despise,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1070f
			</span></i> (dub.l.). (In later Greek 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφ-, ἀφίδω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Phil.</u>
					2.23
				</span></i>
			.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
